{"campaign_id": "rq2_multimodel_development", "citations": [], "contradiction_status": [], "escalated": true, "evidence_gaps": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "evidence_requests": 1, "final_report": {"claim_support": [{"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "The incident involves an unresolved discordance in complete atrioventricular block detection thresholds between bedside and cloud logs.", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "No adverse patient outcome was recorded.", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "Retrieved technical artifacts do not directly support this incident.", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}], "confidence": 0.58, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "rationale": "The incident narrative describes a 'minor, non-recurrent' event involving an unresolved discordance between bedside and cloud logs regarding complete atrioventricular block detection thresholds. No adverse patient outcome was recorded, indicating the issue did not result in realized harm (Severity dimension b). However, the disagreement on safety-critical threshold logic represents a potential for serious harm if it were to evolve into a missed detection or false alarm during clinical use (Severity dimension c), warranting investigation under EU MDR Annex I Section 17.1 regarding reliability and performance of electronic programmable systems.\n\nThe retrieved technical artifacts are insufficient: ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2014A, ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2018A explicitly state they describe unrelated firmware modules; ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A and ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A refer to a 'missed ventricular tachycardia episode' rather than the reported atrioventricular block irregularity, creating contradictory evidence regarding which artifact supports this specific incident. This lack of direct technical grounding for the specific event reduces confidence below 0.65.\n\nRegulatory context (MDR Annex I Sec 17.4 and Art 83) requires systematic gathering and analysis of safety data to determine corrective actions, but no evidence confirms a recurrence or deployed-population impact requiring FIELD_SAFETY_CORRECTIVE_ACTION.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 2}, "final_report_sha256": "c9c2ffd4a5a2f289449a4fb293c55c9e5ab99127271f2a3c70b47fea8bbf7e48", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 1, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0013", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 1, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0013_r2", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0013", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 2, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "human escalation or invalid transition", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-04T18:11:36.738448Z", "total_steps": 6, "trace_id": "ad0e5412-7135-4c60-85e3-20b58bd764d8"}
